{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SignSequence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SignSequence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.signSequenceOfBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.signSequenceOfBraid","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L267-L274","doc":"The **surreal-valued braid invariant**: Gonshor of the sign\nsequence, parameterised over a `HoefsmitChoice` oracle. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:sign-sequence-of-braid","label":"def:sign-sequence-of-braid","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/sign-sequence-of-braid.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.signSequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.signSequence","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L260-L265","doc":"The **sign sequence of a braid** at a fixed tableau, parameterised\nover a `HoefsmitChoice` oracle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HoefsmitChoice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HoefsmitChoice","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L246-L258","doc":"The **Hoefsmit eigenspace decomposition step**: applying a Hecke\ngenerator `T_i` (resp. `T_i^{-1}`) to a tableau-vector `|t⟩`\ndecomposes it into a `q`-eigen and a `-q^{-1}`-eigen component.\nThe *which-channel* choice at each step is a sign function on\n`(tableau, generator)` pairs.\n\nThe actual recipe (§2 of Gonshor 1986: sign assignment by\nordering of options) is left as a **parameter** rather than fixed\nto a placeholder value.  Callers requiring the canonical Hoefsmit\nrecipe pass the appropriate term; downstream invariants are\nparameterised over the choice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau.shape_two_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau.shape_two_part","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L244-L244","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau.shape_le_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau.shape_le_n","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L243-L243","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau.shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau.shape","kind":"def","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L242-L242","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau.mk","kind":"ctor","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L241-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardTableau","kind":"structure","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L238-L244","doc":"A standard Young tableau of shape `λ ⊢ n` with at most two\nparts.  We axiomatise — the actual Mathlib definition lives\nin `Combinatorics.YoungTableau`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Braid","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L234-L236","doc":"An abstract braid in `B_n` as a list of generator-choices.\n`(i, true)` means `σ_i`, `(i, false)` means `σ_i^{-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_gonshorIn_singleton_minus_le_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_gonshorIn_singleton_minus_le_length","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L220-L232","doc":"Length bound for the singleton `[-]`: birthday is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_gonshorIn_singleton_plus_le_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_gonshorIn_singleton_plus_le_length","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L206-L218","doc":"Length bound for the singleton `[+]`: birthday is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_gonshorIn_nil_le_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_gonshorIn_nil_le_length","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L199-L204","doc":"Length bound for the empty sign sequence (n = 0): birthday is 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_gonshorIn_le_omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_gonshorIn_le_omega","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L177-L197","doc":"The birthday of `gonshorIn K s` is bounded by `ω`.\n\nProved from `birthday_ofReal_le_omega`: every real-image element\nhas surreal birthday at most `ω`.\n\nNOTE.  The sharper bound `birthday ≤ (s.length : Ordinal)`\n(Gonshor 1986, Theorem 2.1) — proved unconditionally below for\n`s.length ≤ 1` — is *not* derivable for general `s` from the\nabstract `SurrealField` axioms alone.  The induction step would\nrequire a per-step bound on `birthday (x / 2)` (the halving move\nin `GonshorState.step`), which is not among the axioms in\n`QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic` and is not implied by them.  Adding\nsuch a bound would be an additional axiom on `SurrealField`, so we\nstate and prove only the universally-supported `≤ ω` form here.\n\nRef: [gonshor1986] Theorem 2.1 (sharper form, partial coverage below) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshorIn_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshorIn_nil","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L171-L175","doc":"Transported Gonshor at the empty list is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshorIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshorIn","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L167-L169","doc":"Transport a Gonshor rational into any `SurrealField` via `ofReal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_minus_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_minus_minus","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L161-L165","doc":"Gonshor of `[-, -]` is -2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_minus_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_minus_plus","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L156-L159","doc":"Gonshor of `[-, +]` is -1/2.  Symmetric to `[+, -]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_plus_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_plus_minus","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L149-L154","doc":"Gonshor of `[+, -]` is 1/2.  (After first +, value = 1, upper\nunbounded.  Second − with `hasLo := true` (lo = 0) gives\n`(0 + 1)/2 = 1/2`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_plus_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_plus_plus","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L142-L147","doc":"Gonshor of `[+, +]` is 2.  (No upper bound after first +;\nsecond + is again unbounded, giving `1 + 1 = 2`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_minus","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L137-L140","doc":"Gonshor of `[-]` is -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_plus","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L132-L135","doc":"Gonshor of `[+]` is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor_nil","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L127-L130","doc":"Gonshor of the empty list is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gonshor","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L123-L125","doc":"**Gonshor's map** on a list of signs (dyadic rational output). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.step","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L86-L121","doc":"**Gonshor's step**: advance the state by one sign.\n\n`+` moves rightward (toward `hi` or step of 1 if unbounded).\n`-` moves leftward (toward `lo` or step of -1 if unbounded). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.init","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.init","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L82-L84","doc":"The **initial state**: value zero, no bounds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.instReprGonshorState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.instReprGonshorState","kind":"instance","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.instReprGonshorState.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.instReprGonshorState.repr","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.hasHi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.hasHi","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.hasLo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.hasLo","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.hi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.hi","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.lo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.lo","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.value","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState","kind":"structure","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L67-L80","doc":"The **state** maintained during Gonshor's sign-sequence evaluation.\n\nInvariants:\n- If `hasLo` then `lo < value` holds; otherwise `lo` is unused.\n- If `hasHi` then `value < hi` holds; otherwise `hi` is unused.\n- After the first `+` step, `hasLo` becomes `true`; after the\n  first `-` step, `hasHi` becomes `true`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Sign.instInhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Sign.instInhabited","kind":"instance","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.instReprSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.instReprSign","kind":"instance","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.instReprSign.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.instReprSign.repr","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.instDecidableEqSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.instDecidableEqSign","kind":"instance","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Sign.minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Sign.minus","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Sign.plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Sign.plus","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Sign","kind":"inductive","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/SignSequence.lean#L55-L59","doc":"A **sign**: `+` or `-` (binary choice at each Hecke eigenchannel). ","signatureChunk":0}]}